/-!
# Global strict-tail polynomiality at the joint-weight cutoff

The established origin/Newton argument proves global strict-tail polynomiality
at a coarse schedule degree.  Global polynomiality itself forces the exact
missing-origin equation by uniqueness of polynomial interpolation.  Feeding
that equation back into the sharp successor joint-weight bounds lowers the
global cutoff-profile degree to `cutoff`.

The file is intentionally not imported by the existing collection proof.
