/-!
# Weight-sensitive subsequence coordinates for crossed empty-orbit prefixes

The crossed empty-orbit prefix recurrence appends one flattened fixed-trace
crossing schedule at every step.  Its proper-suffix convolution is triangular
in the requested transition-word length.  Retaining carried weights through
that recurrence gives a sharper polynomial degree bound than the earlier
cutoff-wide estimate.

The file is intentionally not imported by the existing collection proof.
-/

namespace Submission
namespace TCTex
namespace ESWt

